.TH pickles-update 1 "September 7, 2025" "Pickles Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pickles-update - a script to perform system updates on Pickles Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pickles-update
[
.B \-h
|
.B \-\-help
]
[
.B \-v
|
.B \-\-version
]
[
.B \-m
|
.B \-mirrors
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B pickles-update
script automates the process of updating a Pickles Linux system using the
.B paru
package manager. It automatically detects the operating system, updates the package list, and upgrades all installed packages.
.P
The script also provides an optional feature to rate and update the package mirrors for improved download speeds. After the update is complete, the user is prompted to reboot the system.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Displays a help message with the available options and a brief description of the script's functionality.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Displays the version of the
.B pickles-update
script.
.TP
.B \-m, \-mirrors
This option tells the script to run
.B rate-mirrors
before the update. This process rates the available package mirrors and creates a new mirrorlist file, which can lead to faster downloads by using the most responsive mirrors.
.SH EXAMPLES
To simply run a standard system update:
.P
.B pickles-update
.P
To update the system and also rate the mirrors beforehand:
.P
.B pickles-update -m
.P
To display the script's version:
.P
.B pickles-update -v
.SH NOTES
.RS
.IP *
This script requires
.B paru
and
.B rate-mirrors
to be installed on the system.
.IP *
The script must be run with
.B sudo
or as the root user for the updates to be applied.
.IP *
A reboot is often recommended after a significant system update to ensure all changes take effect.
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR paru (1),
.BR rate-mirrors (1)
